{"id":"r6","level":1,"levelName":"Reading","n":6,"of":8,"title":"Vowels: a and e","titleHe":"נִקּוּד: a וְ־e","goal":"Read the four marks that make the a and e sounds.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"Vowels are marks written under (mostly) the consonant they follow. So בַ is read ba, not ab — consonant first, then its vowel. Modern Hebrew has fewer vowel sounds than it has marks, so several marks share a sound."},{"type":"vowels","ids":["ַ","ָ","ֵ","ֶ"],"items":[{"sign":"ַ","on":"בַ","name":"פַּתַח","en":"patach","sound":"a as in father"},{"sign":"ָ","on":"בָ","name":"קָמַץ","en":"kamatz","sound":"a as in father"},{"sign":"ֵ","on":"בֵ","name":"צֵירֵי","en":"tsere","sound":"e as in they"},{"sign":"ֶ","on":"בֶ","name":"סֶגוֹל","en":"segol","sound":"e as in bed"}]},{"type":"tip","body":"פַּתַח and קָמַץ both say a. צֵירֵי and סֶגוֹל both say e. They look different and are spelled differently, but you pronounce each pair the same."}],"vocab":[{"he":"דָּג","en":"fish","translit":"dag"},{"he":"יָם","en":"sea","translit":"yam"},{"he":"אֵם","en":"mother","translit":"em"},{"he":"בֵּן","en":"son","translit":"ben"},{"he":"דֶּלֶת","en":"door","translit":"delet"},{"he":"עֶרֶב","en":"evening","translit":"erev"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What sound does this vowel make?","options":["e as in bed","a as in father","i as in machine","e as in they"],"correct":1,"prompt":"בַ"},{"type":"choice","q":"What sound does this vowel make?","options":["i as in machine","e as in bed","a as in father","e as in they"],"correct":2,"prompt":"בָ"},{"type":"choice","q":"What sound does this vowel make?","options":["a as in father","e as in they","a as in father","e as in bed"],"correct":1,"prompt":"בֵ"},{"type":"choice","q":"What sound does this vowel make?","options":["e as in they","a as in father","a as in father","e as in bed"],"correct":3,"prompt":"בֶ"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["old (of things)","fish","peace","come! (m.)"],"correct":1,"prompt":"דָּג","translit":"dag"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["sea","tomorrow","sings","beginning"],"correct":0,"prompt":"יָם","translit":"yam"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["to him","mother","dog","dad"],"correct":1,"prompt":"אֵם","translit":"em"},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “son”?","options":["בֵּן","קוֹנֶה","לְיַד","כֶּסֶף"],"correct":0,"he":true},{"type":"read","he":"עֶרֶב","translit":"erev","en":"evening"},{"type":"choice","q":"Which mark is patach?","options":["בֶ","בֵ","בַ","בָ"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"read","he":"בֵּן","translit":"ben","en":"son"},{"type":"read","he":"יָם","translit":"yam","en":"sea"},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “evening”?","options":["מְאוֹד","שָׁבוּעַ","שָׁעָה","עֶרֶב"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"Which mark is segol?","options":["בֶ","בַ","בֵ","בָ"],"correct":0,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “sea”?","options":["בֹּקֶר טוֹב","קָם","מְסֻדָּר","יָם"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["עֶרֶב","יָם","דָּג","בֵּן"],"correct":3,"say":"בֵּן","he":true}]}